+# Spec: Create JSON Patch (diff)
+**Standard**: RFC 6902 §4 (operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`), §5 (operations apply in order), with RFC 6901 §3
+(pointer syntax, `~0`/`~1` escaping of member names) and §4 (array indexes). Equality of values follows RFC 6902 §4.6.
+**API**: `createPatch(from, to)` exported from `src/index.ts`; returns an array of operations such that
+`applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to))` deep-equals `to`.
+## Requirements
+- Equal documents give `[]`. Inputs are never modified; the patch shares no structure with them (Constitution IV).
+- Objects: removed members → `remove`, new members → `add`, members present on both sides are compared recursively;
+  an unchanged member produces nothing. Member names are escaped per RFC 6901 §3.
+- Arrays: items are aligned by longest common subsequence, so an inserted item is one `add` and a deleted item one
+  `remove`; the items around it are not touched. An item changed in place is compared recursively (nested change) or
+  replaced. A moved item is a `remove` plus an `add` of it (permitted by the request); items in between are untouched.
+- Different types (or primitives that differ) → `replace` at that path; at the root the path is `""`.
+- Only `add`/`remove`/`replace` are emitted; no `test`, no `-` indexes.
+- `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` are ordinary members; only own members are read.
+- No new error types: every JSON value is valid input.
+## Assumptions
+- Inputs are JSON values. Minimal means "describes only what changed", not a provably shortest patch.
+- Non-breaking addition; README updated.
